 "prop_socket": "Prop_L / Prop_R are keyed to ONE constant local rotation (-90 deg about X) in every clip: socket -Z (Godot forward) points along the fingers / forearm line, +Y (top) to the thumb side. Weapons whose origin is the grip and whose barrel / blade runs along Blender +Y attach with an identity transform. In the bare rest pose (no clip) the socket is identity.",
 "animation_notes": [
  "All clips are in place; 'hips' is the Hips bone position at frame 0, 'speed' the ground speed in m/s a gait covers at 1x playback (use it as NOMINAL_SPEED).",
  "Loop clips end on a copy of frame 0. One-shots hold their last frame.",
  "Every clip owns a rotation track for all 19 bones and a Hips position track that differ from the rest pose (a bone resting for a whole clip is offset by 0.08 deg, a resting Hips by 0.3 mm), so Godot's 'remove_immutable_tracks' import option cannot drop them and an AnimationPlayer never leaves a bone in the previous clip's pose.",
  "AimPistol / AimRifle / HoldRifle / Reload / Punch_* / Stab / Throw / Block keep the Hips un-rotated (at frame 0) so Spine..Hand rotations can be layered over locomotion.",
  "Seated clips (SitCar, SitPassenger, SitBike) are built around the Hips bone = the vehicle seat marker; the pelvis / thigh underside is 0.13 below the Hips bone.",
  "Lying end poses: Death_Back / Knockdown end on the back with the head toward -Y; Death_Front / TakedownVictim end face-down with the head toward +Y; GetUp starts from the Knockdown end pose."
 ],
 "export": {
  "tool": "gta_kit.export_asset(root, 'characters/<id>', animations=True, extra=...)",
  "extra": {
